<!--
     Shared libraries for MediaTek's ImsService (VoLTE).

     ImsService.apk declares five uses-library entries, all with
     required="false": PackageManager adds them to the app classpath only if
     someone has declared them, and does not fail installation when they are
     missing. The names the APK asks for, however, do not match the jars that
     actually hold the classes it uses, so here the five available names are
     mapped onto the right jars.

     What is needed, and why:

       mediatek-ims-base.jar        the ten com.mediatek.ims.internal.IMtkIms* interfaces
       mediatek-common.jar          OperatorCustomizationFactoryLoader
       mediatek-telephony-base.jar  MtkTelephonyManagerEx
       mtk-ims-compat.jar           com.android.ims.ImsServiceBase, which AOSP removed
                                    after Android 10 (it is the stock ROM's
                                    ims-common.jar, installed under another name)

     The first three already come with the blobs: they had always been in
     /system/framework and nobody used them. The fourth is in
     proprietary-files.txt.

     mediatek-ims-legacy.jar and mediatek-ims-common.jar are left out; they most
     likely hold the provisioning that turns on the MMTEL capabilities: the
     uses-library slots have run out, and using them would mean building a
     merged jar. See docs/bringup/volte-stato-esperimento.md
-->
<permissions>
    <library name="com.mediatek.ims.legacy"
             file="/system/framework/mediatek-ims-base.jar" />
    <library name="com.mediatek.ims.plugin"
             file="/system/framework/mediatek-common.jar" />
    <library name="com.mediatek.ims.oemplugin"
             file="/system/framework/mtk-ims-compat.jar" />
    <library name="com.mediatek.op.ims.common"
             file="/system/framework/mediatek-telephony-base.jar" />
</permissions>
